# Speed

In Stencila, a model's score is its throughput. This is measured as the time it
takes to deliver all tokens, divided by the number of tokens in a response. The
time starts once the first token is received.

To assess throughput, we use the open data provided by `thefastest.ai`
benchmarking service. The fastest.ai periodically runs tests against providers'
infrastructure. To calculate the score for each model, we calculate the median
of the 5 most recent tests per provider and region, then take the median of
those scores. This provides us with a way to compare the throughput of models
across different providers.

delivered between the first and last token. This measure is calculated as time
to first token $-$ total time, divided by the number of tokens in the test.

