# Distribution of metrics

::: create @code-chunk [anthropic/claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022] write code to calculate a best fit model of the quality_pct, cost_pct and speed_pct while minimising error. use only pandas and numpy, rather than relying on other packages sklearn. >>>

```python exec
# Create array of predictor variables (cost_pct, speed_pct) and target (quality_pct)
X = df[['cost_pct', 'speed_pct']].values
y = df['quality_pct'].values

# Add column of 1s for intercept term
X = np.column_stack([np.ones(len(X)), X])

# Calculate coefficients using normal equation: beta = (X'X)^-1 X'y
beta = np.linalg.inv(X.T @ X) @ X.T @ y

# Calculate predicted values
y_pred = X @ beta

# Calculate error metrics
mse = np.mean((y - y_pred) ** 2)
rmse = np.sqrt(mse)
r2 = 1 - np.sum((y - y_pred) ** 2) / np.sum((y - np.mean(y)) ** 2)

# Print results
print("Model coefficients:")
print(f"Intercept: {beta[0]:.4f}")
print(f"Cost coefficient: {beta[1]:.4f}") 
print(f"Speed coefficient: {beta[2]:.4f}")
print("\nModel performance:")
print(f"MSE: {mse:.4f}")
print(f"RMSE: {rmse:.4f}")
print(f"R-squared: {r2:.4f}")
```

